{"repositoryId":1097115377,"availability":"available","full":"sarah-majdoub/SmartRestaurantService","name":"SmartRestaurantService","description":"Restaurant table occupancy and service timing from video: YOLO11 detection, pose estimation to spot seated customers, centroid tracking","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"Python","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2025-11-15T15:12:00Z","updated":"2026-10-18T18:25:09Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://sarra-majdoub.vercel.app/projects/smart-restaurant","topics":["computer-vision","object-tracking","opencv","pose-estimation","python","yolo"],"demo":"https://sarra-majdoub.vercel.app/projects/smart-restaurant","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-18T19:18:27.918Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-18T19:18:27.918Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-18T19:18:27.918Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-18T19:18:27.918Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Computer vision that reads restaurant occupancy from a video feed: which tables are free, which are taken, which are \"reserved\" by a bag left on a chair, and how long each table waited to be served.","A table is not free just because nobody is sitting at it. A jacket over a chair or a laptop on the table means someone is coming back. And a person standing next to a table is usually a waiter, not a customer. So the system combines three signals:"],"features":["Object detection (YOLO11x) for people, tables, chairs, sofas, tableware and personal items: bags, phones, laptops, books, umbrellas.","Pose estimation (YOLOv8x-pose) to tell seated customers from passers-by. A person counts as seated when the torso-to-leg ratio of their COCO keypoints drops below 0.55 and the knees are below the hips.","Centroid tracking so each table keeps the same ID across frames, even when it is briefly occluded."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/sarah-majdoub/SmartRestaurantService/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"63167b